WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.771
What this means for the code you write.

2
00:00:02.051 --> 00:00:05.144
Hold on to five working rules as you start building.

3
00:00:05.424 --> 00:00:09.499
Budget in tokens, because tokens are cost, latency, and limits.

4
00:00:09.779 --> 00:00:14.024
Expect variation, so validate every output your code depends on.

5
00:00:14.304 --> 00:00:19.275
Treat context as something you design: what goes in, in what order, and what stays out.

6
00:00:19.555 --> 00:00:22.840
Know your model’s cutoff, and supply current facts yourself.

7
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.387
And evaluate on many examples, because one good answer proves very little.

8
00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:31.315
The next lesson puts these rules to work in your first API calls.
